# The bare-fist hit of a player is rolled with the fist attack a script gives it (O505, owner 2026-11-11, translated: "You can fix these 3 things
# of the auto attack"; server/README.md "Flat armour, weapon spells and the Monk's fist (O505)"). The engine's bare-fist hit is attack 7
# (Weapon::useFist, weapons.cpp): the Monk line and Open Hand Creed rescale it in an event that runs AFTER the monster's own flat armour and
# defence took their part (Creature::blockHit), so at attack 7 nearly all of a Monk's hit died in the flat armour of a monster before the
# scaling (6% of its damage reached a level 100 monster with the monster layer off). Now:
#   * Player::setChaosFist(attack, multiplier) / Lua player:setFistAttack(attack, multiplier) / player:getFistAttack(): the attack value
#     and a multiplier of the maximum hit; attack 0 (or a value outside 0 .. 2000, NaN, infinity) is "none set" and the stock hit stays
#     (a multiplier outside 0 .. 10 is 1). Not saved: the script sets it again after a login.
#   * Weapon::useFist rolls max = round(maxWeaponDamage(level, fist skill, attack, attack factor) x multiplier) when an attack is set,
#     with the stock formula, the player's own fist skill and fight mode, and the stock bell between 0 and max. Without one nothing changes.
#   * The only fist path: Weapon::useFist is the only caller of the bare-fist roll (player.cpp doAttacking when no weapon is in the hands;
#     a Monk's fist weapon is a shield-type item, which Player::getWeapon skips: patch 0087). A weapon in the hands never reaches it.
#   * The capability the scripts detect: type(Player.setFistAttack) == "function". An engine without this patch ignores the scripts'
#     feature test and rolls attack 7 as before.
# New header src/chaosfist.h (pure functions, tests in server/tools/chaosfist_test.cpp, CI).
# Apply in the server source root after 0001-0090: patch -p1 --fuzz=0 < 0091-fist-attack-from-script.patch, then rebuild.
